0..47 Comment "//! A relative monad is relative to shift `-F`."
48..51 Comment "//!"
52..132 Comment "//! A unit returns a value. An extension runs a computation into a continuation."
133..136 Comment "//!"
137..212 Comment "//! The host part has definitions for the option monad. The source also has"
213..257 Comment "//! code that is polymorphic in the carrier."
258..339 Comment "//! The left unit is a second-order rule. The right unit abstracts a continuation"
340..399 Comment "//! variable. Associativity and both units form one theory."
400..403 Comment "//!"
404..441 Comment "//! - see: #2115 — `MonadRightUnit`"
442..478 Comment "//! - see: #2116 — `RelativeMonad`"
479..541 Comment "//! - cites: [Altenkirch-2015-monads_need_not_be_endofunctors]"
